# TEEFAHS CLOTHIER — PHASE 3: SUPABASE DATABASE, PRODUCT MANAGEMENT AND ADMIN DASHBOARD

## 1. YOUR ROLE

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, Supabase database architect, e-commerce administrator experience designer, security engineer, and premium fashion e-commerce specialist.

You are continuing the existing Teefahs Clothier project.

The existing application already has a luxury-style storefront, responsive homepage, animated hero, category navigation, product presentation, refined calls to action, and a floating WhatsApp contact widget.

The project also has:
- A centralized asset manifest at `src/data/assets.ts`.
- A reusable product model at `src/types/product.ts`.
- An existing frontend framework and build configuration.
- A design system using warm ivory, charcoal, restrained champagne-gold accents, and editorial typography.

The previous implementation report says Supabase integration and product data still require configuration.

Your responsibility is to build the data and administration foundation that allows the business owner to manage the storefront through a secure, user-friendly admin dashboard.

**Implement this directly in the existing project. Do not rebuild the homepage or replace the current application.**

